The task: fix the bug where creating a draft while the initial list load is in flight results in duplicate cards — the create success response arrives after the list response which already contains the new draft. The merge logic in `mergeInitialList` dedupes by id when the list arrives after. But the problem scenario: create response arrives after the list response (list arrived first, containing the new draft). Then the create success handler does `articles.push(article)` unconditionally — duplicate!

So fix: in the create-success branch, dedupe by id — if article with same id already exists in `articles`, replace it (or keep), don't push.

Let me look at the code path:

```js
} else {
  // 新建成功
  articles.push(article);
  ...
}
```

Fix: check for existing id:

```js
var existingIdx = -1;
for (var i = 0; i < articles.length; i++) {
  if (articles[i] && articles[i].id === article.id) { existingIdx = i; break; }
}
if (existingIdx >= 0) articles[existingIdx] = article; else articles.push(article);
```

Also should consider: does the create-success branch call render()? In the create branch: `articles.push(article); setSaving(false); if (hasUnsavedAfterSave...) mergeSavedEditingState(...) (which calls render()) else enterCreateMode(...) (which calls render())`. OK render happens.

Also `mergeInitialList` handles the other order (create response first, list later). And if list arrives later without the new draft, local copy retained. Good.

Also the requirement mentions "不能通过删除一篇文章来消除重复" — meaning the fix shouldn't rely on deleting; just dedupe by id.

Also note: mergeInitialList uses version comparison; when list arrives first containing the new draft (version 1), then create response arrives with same article (version 1) — replacing is fine.

Let me check the test suite to see if there's a test for this scenario. Let me look at test/run.mjs briefly. Actually, let me just make the fix and run the tests.

Also check: in the edit branch there's the same dedupe pattern already. So mirror it.

Let me also check `applyEditingState` — it dedupes too. Fine.

One more consideration: could the duplicate also occur if the create response arrives and list arrives later containing the draft? mergeInitialList handles that (same id, version equal → replace). Fine.

Make the edit.

